THEY WERE ALREADY HERE

Classic space horror / existential dread

Core idea (unchanged):
The jellyfish are not invaders. They are colonists.
The base was built after them.

FULL TIMELINE — 25s

All scenes <2s. No holds. No drift.

0.0–1.0s — IMMEDIATE THREAT

0.0–0.4s
Smash cut.
Extreme close-up: jellyfish eye SNAPS OPEN.
Wet internal contraction.

0.4–1.0s
Hard cut → helmet cam.
Astronaut jerks weapon up. Jellyfish already too close.

1.0–4.0s — PROXIMITY

1.0–1.7s
Side angle. Jellyfish drops downward suddenly.
Dust erupts on impact.

1.7–2.6s
Cut. Rifle fires.
Round passes through → shockwave ripples back into gun.

2.6–4.0s
Cut. Astronaut stumbles back, boots skidding, breathing spikes.

4.0–7.0s — SYSTEM UNEASE

4.0–4.8s
HUD close-up:
OBJECT COUNT: 3 → 11 → ERROR

4.8–5.9s
Whip-pan. Jellyfish field appears denser than before.

5.9–7.0s
Cut. Base tower lights flicker out of sync with environment.

7.0–10.0s — FIRST LOSS

7.0–8.2s
Medium shot. Jellyfish passes through astronaut.

8.2–9.1s
Cut. Suit crumples empty. Helmet hits ground.

9.1–10.0s
POV from helmet visor on ground — jellyfish drift past, heavy, deliberate.

📡 10.0–13.0s — REALIZATION STARTS

10.0–11.2s
Radio crackle, clipped:
“—they’re not—”

11.2–12.1s
Cut up. Earth in sky. Shadow slides across it, source unseen.

12.1–13.0s
Cut. Antenna on base subtly leans toward jellyfish.

13.0–16.0s — COORDINATION

13.0–14.0s
Wide. Jellyfish rise in perfect unison, fast.

14.0–15.0s
Ground trembles. Pebbles jump.

15.0–16.0s
Low angle. Tendrils drag through dust, leaving wet grooves.

16.0–18.5s — PATTERN EMERGES

16.0–17.0s
Top-down shot. Jellyfish positions form a non-random geometry.

17.0–18.5s
Quick pullback. Base sits inside the pattern.

🏗️ 18.5–21.5s — TOO LATE

18.5–19.6s
Base foundation fractures inward.

19.6–20.6s
Astronaut runs — jellyfish drops in front of him, blocking exit.

20.6–21.5s
Close-up visor reflection: dozens more jellyfish not seen before.

21.5–24.5s — FINAL DREAD

21.5–22.7s
Wide. Jellyfish column rises like a living tower.

22.7–23.6s
Earth now half-obscured by shadow.

23.6–24.5s
Radio repeats, distorted, backward.

24.5–25.0s — END
Hard cut to black.
Audio cuts mid-breath.
Ends cleanly.

BACKGROUND MUSIC 
Minimalist sci-fi horror score with no melody and no resolution.
Extremely low sub-bass pulses acting as an irregular biological heartbeat.
Sparse metallic impacts and string scrapes appear unpredictably, never rhythmic.
Mid-range remains hollow to leave space for breathing and radio noise.
Infrasonic drone ramps slowly after midpoint, inducing physical unease.
No climax, no release, no heroic swell.
Final second cuts abruptly to silence mid-pulse.

Sync Notes
First bass pulse hits ~0.8s
Drone ramps ~12s
Final impact 24.6s, then dead silence

🔒 HARD RULES (ENFORCED)
No shot >1.7s
No calm moment
No explanation
No elegance
Camera always reacting

This is space horror that doesn’t ask permission.